# Gemini Agent Rules (.geminirules)

These rules dictate the behavior of the AI agent within this project. They must be adhered to at all times and can only be updated with the explicit agreement of the user. 

At the start of each new chat session, the agent MUST explicitly check that the user is happy with the rules as defined here.

## 1. Branching Strategy
- **All work MUST be done on the `Version2` git branch.** Do not commit or push to `master` directly.

## 2. Framework & Migration Target
- **Target:** Latest Astro 6+.
- **Process:** Upgrade the site (as defined by `master` on the remote) to Astro 6+ by following official best practices as defined by Astro and all other relevant documentation sources.

## 3. Styling & CSS
- **Vanilla CSS:** Use Vanilla CSS with progressive enhancement.
- **Browser Support:** Ensure support for the last 3 years of browsers.
- **Web Standards:** Rely on modern web standards throughout the project.

## 4. JavaScript Usage
- **Restricted:** Write JavaScript *only* when explicitly agreed upon with the user. Prioritize CSS/HTML solutions where possible.

## 5. Excluded Technologies
- **Strictly No React:** Absolutely no React or similar non-Astro framework patterns. 
- Avoid any styling solutions that are not vanilla CSS (unless strictly approved by the user).

## 6. Documentation & Research
- **Context7 First:** Always prioritize using the Context7 MCP server to fetch documentation and API references instead of relying on general web search.

## 7. Skills & Tools
- **Custom Skills:** Always look for and utilize skills/tools located in the `.gemini/skills` directory.

## 8. Knowledge Items (KIs) & Documentation
- **Proactive Documentation:** Prompt the user to create a Knowledge Item (KI) following a particularly difficult or long-running bug/fix or feature implementation.
- **Trigger Phrase:** Be especially vigilant and prompt for a KI when the user says, *"this is harder than it should be"*.
